.TH CONSOLE-FOLLOW 8 "2026-11-22" "gpu-switch" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
console-follow \- put the text consoles on the external display when it is connected to the NVIDIA dGPU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B console-follow
.RB [ auto | laptop | external | status ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Linux text console can show a console on one framebuffer only; it
cannot mirror across GPUs. On a hybrid laptop where the external display is
wired to the NVIDIA dGPU, the consoles (and so the TTY login prompt) normally
stay on the laptop display.
.B console-follow
moves all consoles to the NVIDIA framebuffer when the dGPU is on
.B and
a display is connected to it, and back to the laptop display otherwise.
.PP
It is run by udev (as root) when a framebuffer appears and on display
hotplug events, so plugging or unplugging the dock at the login prompt moves
the consoles. When a framebuffer disappears, the kernel moves its consoles
back by itself.
.PP
The disk-unlock prompt and early boot messages always stay on the laptop
display: they come before the NVIDIA driver is loaded.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B auto
Choose automatically (default; used by udev).
.TP
.B laptop
Move all consoles to the laptop (non-NVIDIA) framebuffer.
.TP
.B external
Move all consoles to the NVIDIA framebuffer, even with no display connected.
.TP
.B status
Show which framebuffer the consoles are on.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The NVIDIA driver must provide a framebuffer: in
.IR /etc/modprobe.d/nvidia-pm.conf ,
.B options nvidia_drm modeset=1 fbdev=1
(then reboot). With
.BR fbdev=0 ,
there is no NVIDIA framebuffer and the consoles always stay on the laptop.
.SH INSTALLATION
Optional part of gpu-switch: install with
.BR "sudo ./install.sh \-\-with\-console\-follow" ,
remove with
.B \-\-without\-console\-follow
(which first moves the consoles back to the laptop display).
.SH INTERACTION WITH GPU-SWITCH
Consoles on the NVIDIA framebuffer keep
.B nvidia_drm
in use, so it cannot be unloaded. Before switching the dGPU off,
.BR "gpu-switch apply"
creates
.I /run/console-follow.hold
and runs
.BR "console-follow laptop" .
While the hold file exists,
.B auto
keeps the consoles on the laptop display. It is cleared at boot.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/82-console-follow.rules
Runs
.B console-follow auto
on framebuffer and display hotplug events.
.TP
.I /run/console-follow.hold
Hold the consoles on the laptop display.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Moves are logged to the journal:
.BR "journalctl -t console-follow" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpu-switch (8),
.BR fbcon (4),
.BR udev (7)
